{
    "file": "Coaching_Salespeople.docx",
    "title": "Coaching Salespeople",
    "duration": "3 Days",
    "overview": [
        "Coaching salespeople is a core leadership responsibility that improves selling behaviors, builds capability, and supports consistent commercial performance. Effective sales coaching goes beyond checking targets or giving instructions: it uses observation, questioning, feedback, practice, and follow-up to help salespeople develop their own judgment and execution.",
        "This three-day course provides sales managers and team leaders with a structured, practical approach to coaching individuals across the sales cycle. Participants learn to diagnose performance gaps, distinguish coaching from performance management, conduct productive one-to-ones, observe customer interactions, use sales data appropriately, develop specific skills, and sustain behavioral improvement.",
        "The course uses realistic sales cases, coaching role plays, pipeline reviews, call-observation exercises, and individual coaching plans to help participants turn everyday sales activity into opportunities for learning and measurable performance improvement."
    ],
    "audience": [
        "Sales managers, sales supervisors, team leaders, regional and branch sales managers, business-development managers, key account team leaders, field sales managers, inside-sales leaders, and experienced sales professionals preparing to coach others."
    ],
    "methodology": [
        "Interactive presentations, facilitated discussion, sales-performance case analysis, coaching demonstrations, structured questioning exercises, sales-call observation, role plays, feedback practice, peer coaching, pipeline review simulations, and practical coaching action plans."
    ],
    "competencies": [
        "Sales coaching and development",
        "Performance diagnosis",
        "Coaching conversations",
        "Active listening and questioning",
        "Behavioral observation",
        "Constructive feedback",
        "Sales-skill development",
        "Goal setting and accountability",
        "Motivation and engagement",
        "Pipeline coaching",
        "Coaching documentation",
        "Continuous performance improvement"
    ],
    "objectivesIntro": [
        "By the end of the course, participants will be able to:"
    ],
    "objectives": [
        "Explain how coaching differs from directing, training, and performance appraisal.",
        "Identify the sales behaviors and capabilities that influence commercial results.",
        "Diagnose performance gaps using relevant activity, conversion, and outcome evidence.",
        "Plan and conduct structured one-to-one sales coaching conversations.",
        "Use active listening and powerful questions to develop salesperson ownership.",
        "Observe sales calls and provide specific, actionable feedback.",
        "Coach key stages of the sales process, including discovery, value communication, objection handling, and closing.",
        "Adapt coaching approaches to different experience and performance levels.",
        "Set focused development goals and agree practical follow-up actions.",
        "Use pipeline reviews as developmental conversations rather than status checks.",
        "Evaluate whether coaching produces changes in behavior and performance.",
        "Develop a realistic coaching rhythm and individual coaching action plan."
    ],
